{"parentUuid":"da7ecea7-2c9f-4536-80fc-e54c439f6c95","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace/data","sessionId":"b9bd4d98-27a2-48ab-ac41-32e817baad27","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"a219cdb","slug":"majestic-gliding-spring","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01SWVbVCYP4nCXKMMhxxMXdx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Google Cluster Data 2011 schema task events job events CSV columns\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cluster-data/ClusterData2011_2.md at master · google/cluster-data\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/ClusterData2011_2.md\"},{\"title\":\"Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.01426\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/cluster-data: Borg cluster traces from Google\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cluster Trace Dataset Overview\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/google-cluster-trace-dataset\"},{\"title\":\"First Steps Exploring the Google Cluster dataset with iPython | Mark Stillwell\",\"url\":\"https://stillwell.me/~mark/post/first-steps-exploring-the-google-cluster-dataset-with-ipython/\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cluster Usage Traces | PDF | Computer Data Storage | Scheduling (Computing)\",\"url\":\"https://www.scribd.com/document/901116490/Google-Cluster-Usage-Traces\"},{\"title\":\"Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema Charles Reiss, John Wilkes\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Auday-Al-Dulaimy/post/Are-there-any-datasets-for-cloudSim/attachment/59d61de379197b807797be3e/AS:273823268573184@1442295962733/download/Google+cluster+usage+traces.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google Cluster Trace based on Resource Usage\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/270593953_Analysis_and_Clustering_of_Workload_in_Google_Cluster_Trace_based_on_Resource_Usage\"},{\"title\":\"Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema\",\"url\":\"https://t1.daumcdn.net/cfile/tistory/26542633597592552C\"},{\"title\":\"Analyzing Traces from a Google Data Center\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-01870216/file/analyzing-traces-google.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I can provide you with information about the Google Cluster Data 2011 schema for task events and job events CSV columns:\n\n## Task Events CSV Columns\n\nThe task event CSV files contain the fields: 'time', 'missing info', 'job ID', 'task index', 'machine_id', 'event type', 'user', 'scheduling class', 'priority', 'cpu request', 'memory request', 'disk space request', 'different machines restriction'.\n\nThis table is represented by thirteen columns which include fields such as time stamp, missing information, index of tasks, event type, priority of a task which can be free priorities or a production priority.\n\n## Job Events Information\n\nJob events table contains fields like timestamp, a field in missing information, type of event, a scheduling class which represents latency sensitivity of a job or task, name of job which is mostly unique and generated.\n\n## Event Types\n\nEvent types include: SUBMIT (0) - A task or job became eligible for scheduling; SCHEDULE (1) - A job or task was scheduled on a machine; FINISH (4) - A task or job completed normally.\n\n## General Context\n\nThe clusterdata-2011-2 trace represents 29 day's worth of Borg cell information from May 2011, on a cluster of about 12.5k machines.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"594f9e54-7a78-4213-bbc9-cf266845a006","timestamp":"2026-01-29T05:51:52.864Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"da7ecea7-2c9f-4536-80fc-e54c439f6c95"}
