{"parentUuid":"aa61adc4-9474-4d5f-8eae-9517ccce0fef","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace/data","sessionId":"b9bd4d98-27a2-48ab-ac41-32e817baad27","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"a219cdb","slug":"majestic-gliding-spring","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_014T6YCebZyRAPygFEevizdk","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"clusterdata_trace_format_v3.proto Google Cluster Data task job events\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cluster-data/clusterdata_trace_format_v3.proto at master · google/cluster-data\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/clusterdata_trace_format_v3.proto\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/cluster-data: Borg cluster traces from Google\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data\"},{\"title\":\"cluster-data/ClusterData2011_2.md at master · google/cluster-data\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/ClusterData2011_2.md\"},{\"title\":\"Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.01426\"},{\"title\":\"cluster-data/bibliography.bib at master · google/cluster-data\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/bibliography.bib\"},{\"title\":\"cluster-data/ClusterData2019.md at master · google/cluster-data\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/ClusterData2019.md\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cluster Trace Dataset Overview\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/google-cluster-trace-dataset\"},{\"title\":\"cluster-data/TraceVersion1.md at master · google/cluster-data\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/TraceVersion1.md\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google Cluster Trace based on Resource Usage\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/270593953_Analysis_and_Clustering_of_Workload_in_Google_Cluster_Trace_based_on_Resource_Usage\"},{\"title\":\"Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema\",\"url\":\"https://t1.daumcdn.net/cfile/tistory/26542633597592552C\"}]\n\nI found the search results for the `clusterdata_trace_format_v3.proto` file. Here's what I found:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe file uses proto2 syntax and is part of the google.cluster_data package. This is a Protocol Buffer definition file that describes the format for Google's cluster trace data.\n\n## Key Components\n\nThe file defines a Resources structure for CPU and memory resource units, with normalized GCUs (NCUs) for CPUs and normalized RAM bytes for memory.\n\nCollections in the schema are either jobs (which have tasks) or alloc sets (which have alloc instances).\n\n## Context\n\nThis proto file is part of version 3 (aka ClusterData2019), which provides data from eight Borg cells over the month of May 2019. \n\nThe dataset includes six principal CSV tables: machine events, machine attributes, job events, task events, task constraints, and task (instance) resource usage.\n\nThe protocol buffer file is available in the Google cluster-data repository on GitHub, and the data and trace documentation are made available under the CC-BY license.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8d6ec428-2cb5-4b80-9dab-d61fb1da308f","timestamp":"2026-01-29T05:52:06.954Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aa61adc4-9474-4d5f-8eae-9517ccce0fef"}
