{"parentUuid":"8e2f22e5-85ee-4a21-b032-f1289322a97c","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace/data","sessionId":"b9bd4d98-27a2-48ab-ac41-32e817baad27","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"a219cdb","slug":"majestic-gliding-spring","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_vrtx_01J2PBSu3oKrPgVxomefFGyi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01DLz8J3AUjLbSAzhS9Kzrn3","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/clusterdata_trace_format_v3.proto","prompt":"What are the task events and job events message structures with field names and types?"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":887,"cache_read_input_tokens":44862,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":887,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXb9Z9u6geM2hTEbMKv9k","type":"assistant","uuid":"7201c3d3-94ad-49d2-bb4c-8c784e0911e8","timestamp":"2026-01-29T05:52:08.931Z"}
{"parentUuid":"7201c3d3-94ad-49d2-bb4c-8c784e0911e8","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace/data","sessionId":"b9bd4d98-27a2-48ab-ac41-32e817baad27","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"a219cdb","slug":"majestic-gliding-spring","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01DLz8J3AUjLbSAzhS9Kzrn3","type":"tool_result","content":"# Task and Job Event Structures\n\nBased on the Protocol Buffer file, Google's cluster trace format defines events through two primary message types:\n\n## InstanceEvent (Tasks)\nRepresents individual task events with these fields:\n- `time` (int64): Timestamp in microseconds\n- `type` (EventType): Event classification\n- `collection_id` (int64): Parent job identifier\n- `scheduling_class` (LatencySensitivity): Latency sensitivity level\n- `missing_type` (MissingType): Data completeness indicator\n- `collection_type` (CollectionType): Job or alloc set designation\n- `priority` (int32): Scheduling priority\n- `instance_index` (int32): Position within collection\n- `machine_id` (int64): Machine placement identifier\n- `resource_request` (Resources): CPU and memory requirements\n- `constraint` (repeated MachineConstraint): Placement constraints\n\n## CollectionEvent (Jobs)\nApplies to jobs as a whole with these fields:\n- `time` (int64): Timestamp in microseconds\n- `type` (EventType): Event classification\n- `collection_id` (int64): Job identifier\n- `scheduling_class` (LatencySensitivity): Latency sensitivity\n- `priority` (int32): Scheduling priority\n- `user` (string): Job owner\n- `collection_name` (string): Obfuscated job name\n- `max_per_machine` (int32): Instance placement limit\n- `scheduler` (Scheduler): Scheduler type assignment\n\nBoth structures share common event types including SUBMIT, SCHEDULE, EVICT, FAIL, FINISH, and KILL."}]},"uuid":"677f5b65-fe96-43d3-b489-075c09f7c7ee","timestamp":"2026-01-29T05:52:14.091Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7201c3d3-94ad-49d2-bb4c-8c7