{"parentUuid":"9d32cee2-d510-4a86-a83e-107ab41d10e8","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace/data","sessionId":"b9bd4d98-27a2-48ab-ac41-32e817baad27","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"a219cdb","slug":"majestic-gliding-spring","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_0164X6HgwMt1eqr728DtGRAw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"task events\" CSV columns \"time\" \"job_id\" \"task_id\" \"event_type\" Google Cluster 2011\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"First Steps Exploring the Google Cluster dataset with iPython | Mark Stillwell\",\"url\":\"https://stillwell.me/~mark/post/first-steps-exploring-the-google-cluster-dataset-with-ipython/\"},{\"title\":\"Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.01426\"},{\"title\":\"cluster-data/ClusterData2011_2.md at master · google/cluster-data\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/ClusterData2011_2.md\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cluster Trace Dataset Overview\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/google-cluster-trace-dataset\"},{\"title\":\"Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema Charles Reiss, John Wilkes\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Auday-Al-Dulaimy/post/Are-there-any-datasets-for-cloudSim/attachment/59d61de379197b807797be3e/AS:273823268573184@1442295962733/download/Google+cluster+usage+traces.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cluster Usage Traces | PDF | Computer Data Storage | Scheduling (Computing)\",\"url\":\"https://www.scribd.com/document/901116490/Google-Cluster-Usage-Traces\"},{\"title\":\"Analyzing Traces from a Google Data Center\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-01870216/file/analyzing-traces-google.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Tasks log events - Google Workspace Admin Help\",\"url\":\"https://support.google.com/a/answer/12929031?hl=en\"},{\"title\":\"Fixing the time of some tasks (e.g. meetings)\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/taskjuggler-users/c/t8L4k04RaXU\"},{\"title\":\"Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema\",\"url\":\"https://t1.daumcdn.net/cfile/tistory/26542633597592552C\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found detailed information about the task events CSV columns in the Google Cluster 2011 dataset:\n\nThe task event CSV files contain the fields 'time', 'missing info', 'job ID', 'task index', 'machine_id', 'event type', 'user', 'scheduling class', 'priority', 'cpu request', 'memory request', 'disk space request', 'different machines restriction'.\n\nThe specific columns you mentioned are all present in this schema:\n- **time** - the timestamp of the event\n- **job_id** (referred to as 'job ID' in the documentation)\n- **task_id** (referred to as 'task index' in the documentation)\n- **event_type** (referred to as 'event type')\n\nThe 'job ID' and 'task index' fields are needed to keep track of the evolution of a given task over time.\n\nThe Google cluster trace is a dataset released by Google in May 2011 and contains cell information of about 29 days, and the clusterdata-2011-2 trace represents 29 day's worth of Borg cell information from May 2011, on a cluster of about 12.5k machines.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cbea6fe1-f084-4822-b6d1-dcd319b27954","timestamp":"2026-01-29T05:52:22.153Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9d32cee2-d510-4a86-a83e-107ab41d10e8"}
