{"parentUuid":"6e6eb5a2-f1cf-4d42-b269-79730ca84e6c","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace/data","sessionId":"b9bd4d98-27a2-48ab-ac41-32e817baad27","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"a219cdb","slug":"majestic-gliding-spring","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01KNr9CrCCNhxs9kVfjtwU2w","type":"tool_result","content":"# Job Events CSV Column Order\n\nAccording to the documentation, the job_events CSV contains five columns in this order:\n\n1. **init_time** - Start time value relative to the granularity setting\n2. **finish_time** - End time value relative to the granularity setting\n3. **timestamp_1** - First of two subsequent logs used for inter-arrival calculation\n4. **timestamp_2** - Second of two subsequent logs used for inter-arrival calculation\n5. **inter_time** - The calculated inter-arrival duration\n\nThe repository states: \"those are time values considered with respect to the granularity\" for the first two columns, while the timestamp fields represent consecutive log entries analyzed to determine arrival rates."}]},"uuid":"6e9f0890-026b-49bf-a979-738556e3e147","timestamp":"2026-01-29T05:52:43.599Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6e6eb5a2-f1cf-4d42-b269-79730ca84e6c"}
