{"parentUuid":"410934e5-12da-4975-bc5a-915c020dafff","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace/data","sessionId":"b9bd4d98-27a2-48ab-ac41-32e817baad27","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"a219cdb","slug":"majestic-gliding-spring","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01AVoW2X8atKY5npX86X3t3w","type":"tool_result","content":"Total columns: 8\nCol 1: [5620274759]\nCol 2: []\nCol 3: [6252007148]\nCol 4: [4]\nCol 5: [AL1ptJgzhEaoLf97k5xU6Uc2VO0yUaPQd/feJ5LMWhA=]\nCol 6: [0]\nCol 7: [v9ts2JYvO1mIA0WIprzcfG/VuLV2+k4Q7RBlLP47TiI=]\nCol 8: [8eJUX2smexw6vuP11WVFleSoOZQT7UEsTxYigrSyMjw=]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"dbd7a19f-da03-40bc-93a1-4f19a3eb40c5","timestamp":"2026-01-29T05:53:37.533Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"410934e5-12da-4975-bc5a-915c020dafff"}
{"parentUuid":"dbd7a19f-da03-40bc-93a1-4f19a3eb40c5","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace/data","sessionId":"b9bd4d98-27a2-48ab-ac41-32e817baad27","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"a219cdb","slug":"majestic-gliding-spring","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_vrtx_011b3cLJwrJYptDTWPZt76qr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive summary based on the data analysis and the documentation I found.\n\n## Summary\n\nBased on my analysis of the `/app/workspace/data/format.pdf` and `/app/workspace/data/ClusterData2011_2.md` files, along with the actual CSV data samples, here is the complete Google Cluster Data 2011-2 schema:\n\n### Task Events CSV Schema\n\n**File Location:** `/app/workspace/data/task_events/part-00001-of-00500.csv.gz`\n\n**Total Columns:** 13\n\n**Column Names and Order (with data types):**\n\n1. `time` - int64 (timestamp in microseconds since epoch)\n2. `missing_info` - string/object (indicates missing or incomplete data)\n3. `job_id` - int64 (unique job identifier)\n4. `task_idx` - int32 (task index/ID within the job)\n5. `machine_id` - int64 (machine identifier where task was scheduled)\n6. `event_type` - int32 (event type code: SUBMIT=0, SCHEDULE=1, EVICT=2, FAIL=3, FINISH=4, KILL=5, LOST=6, etc.)\n7. `user` - string/object (hashed user/owner identifier)\n8. `scheduling_class` - int32 (scheduling class/latency sensitivity)\n9. `priority` - int32 (job priority, 0-11 range)\n10. `cpu_requested` - float64 (CPU resource request in normalized units)\n11. `memory_requested` - float64 (memory resource request in bytes)\n12. `disk_space_requested` - float64 (disk space request)\n13. `different_machines_restriction` - int32 (constraint flag)\n\n**Key Columns for Your Questions:**\n- **Timestamp (microseconds):** Column 1 - `time`\n- **Job ID:** Column 3 - `job_id`\n- **Task ID:** Column 4 - `task_idx`\n- **Event Type:** Column 6 - `event_type`\n\n### Job Events CSV Schema\n\n**File Location:** `/app/workspace/data/job_events/part-00001-of-00500.csv.gz`\n\n**Total Columns:** 8\n\n**Column Names and Order (with data types):**\n\n1. `time` - int64 (timestamp in microseconds since epoch)\n2. `missing_info` - string/object (indicates missing or incomplete data)\n3. `job_id` - int64 (unique job identifier)\n4. `event_type` - int32 (event type code: SUBMIT=0, FINISH=4, FAIL=3, KILL=5, etc.)\n5. `user` - string/object (hashed user/owner identifier)\n6. `scheduling_class` - int32 (scheduling class/latency sensitivity)\n7. `collection_name` - string/object (hashed job name)\n8. `priority` - int32 (job priority, 0-11 range)\n\n**Key Columns for Your Questions:**\n- **Timestamp (microseconds):** Column 1 - `time`\n- **Job ID:** Column 3 - `job_id`\n- **Event Type:** Column 4 - `event_type`\n\n### Event Type Values\n\nBoth task and job events use the following event type codes:\n- `0` = SUBMIT (job/task became eligible for scheduling)\n- `1` = SCHEDULE (job/task was scheduled on a machine)\n- `2` = EVICT (task was evicted from the machine)\n- `3` = FAIL (job/task failed)\n- `4` = FINISH (job/task completed normally)\n- `5` = KILL (job/task was killed)\n- `6` = LOST (task was lost)\n\n### Important Notes\n\n- Both timestamps are in **microseconds** since the Unix epoch\n- Missing data fields are empty strings when data is complete; approximately 0.013% of task events and 0.0008% of job events have non-empty missing_info fields\n- User identifiers and collection names are hashed for privacy\n- Priority values range from 0 to 11, where 0-1 are \"free\" priorities, 9-11 are \"production\" priorities\n- The scheduling_class indicates latency sensitivity of jobs/tasks\n\n### Files Referenced\n\n- **Task Events Data:** `/app/workspace/data/task_events/part-00001-of-00500.csv.gz`\n- **Job Events Data:** `/app/workspace/data/job_events/part-00001-of-00500.csv.gz`\n- **Documentation:** `/app/workspace/data/ClusterData2011_2.md`\n- **Format Specification:** `/app/workspace/data/format.pdf`\n\nSources:\n- [First Steps Exploring the Google Cluster dataset with iPython](https://stillwell.me/~mark/post/first-steps-exploring-the-google-cluster-dataset-with-ipython/)\n- [GitHub - google/cluster-data: Borg cluster traces from Google](https://github.com/google/cluster-data)\n- [Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema](https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Auday-Al-Dulaimy/post/Are-there-any-datasets-for-cloudSim/attachment/59d61de379197b807797be3e/AS:273823268573184@1442295962733/download/Google+cluster+usage+traces.pdf)\n- [clusterdata_trace_format_v3.proto at master · google/cluster-data](https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/clusterdata_trace_format_v3.proto)\n- [Google Cluster Trace Dataset Overview](https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/google-cluster-trace-dataset)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":370,"cache_read_input_tokens":54924,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":370,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXb9fqaUUBMQnWRVNXwW7","type":"assistant","uuid":"94c8b65f-0d54-4f7f-9df3-3ee6418243a4","timestamp":"2026-01-29T05:53:48.585Z"}
